<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20971] lfs find: buffer overflow in parallel find on deep directory trees</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20971</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;With parallel find, a deep directory tree makes the worker threads write past the end of a heap buffer. As soon as a directory path is longer than about PATH_MAX - NAME_MAX, the names of its entries are appended past the end of a PATH_MAX + 1 allocation. Note the serial traversal does not have the problem.&lt;br/&gt;
Also, a directory path longer than PATH_MAX is silently truncated by the snprintf() in work_unit_create(), while the serial traversal handles such paths (up to 2 * PATH_MAX).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer, on a client with /mnt/lustre mounted (16 nested directories with 250-character names give a 4035-character directory path, plus a file with a 200-character name inside the deepest one):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;B=/mnt/lustre/deep; mkdir -p $B; cd $B
c=$(printf "c%.0s" $(seq 1 250))
for i in $(seq 1 16); do mkdir $c &amp;amp;&amp;amp; cd $c; done
touch $(printf "f%.0s" $(seq 1 200))
cd /
lfs find $B &amp;gt; /dev/null
valgrind -q lfs find --threads 4 $B &amp;gt; /dev/null
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;"lfs find $B" is aborted by glibc:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;double free or corruption (!prev)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;and valgrind reports the overflow:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Invalid write of size 1
   at 0x4871880: strcpy (vg_replace_strmem.c:565)
   by 0x48BD4E3: llapi_semantic_traverse (liblustreapi_pfind.c:3303)
   by 0x48BD9F3: find_worker (liblustreapi_pfind.c:3442)
   by 0x4B81E97: start_thread (in /usr/lib64/libc.so.6)
   by 0x4BEC61B: thread_start (in /usr/lib64/libc.so.6)
 Address 0x50df3a1 is 0 bytes after a block of size 4,097 alloc'd
   at 0x48684C8: malloc (vg_replace_malloc.c:447)
   by 0x48BD283: work_unit_create (liblustreapi_pfind.c:3785)
   by 0x48BD283: work_unit_create_and_add (liblustreapi_pfind.c:3817)
   by 0x48BD65B: llapi_semantic_traverse (liblustreapi_pfind.c:3328)
   by 0x48BD9F3: find_worker (liblustreapi_pfind.c:3442)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
